[Metro Board file 2026-0577, Contract]
AUTHORIZE the Chief Executive Officer to:

A.	AWARD Contract No. OP118576(2)000 with ElDorado National (California), Inc. (ENC), for the manufacturing and delivery of 220 Battery Electric Buses (BEBs) in the amount of $337,698,727.58 for the base contract, including taxes and delivery; exclusive of any contract option buses, subject to the resolution of any properly submitted protest(s), if any;

B.	INCREASE the Life-Of-Project (LOP) for Capital Project 201078 from $52,000,000, established to purchase up to 40 BEBs under the Washington State contract, by $382,355,185 to purchase up to 220 Battery Electric Buses (BEBs) and provide funding for professional and technical support, internal labor, and contingencies, for a total LOP of $434,355,185; and 

C.	NEGOTIATE AND EXECUTE future contract modifications to the contract up to $1,000,000.

BASS AMENDMENT: Direct the CEO to:

A.	AWARD the base contract of 220 Battery Electric Buses (BEBs) to El Dorado Nation Inc.; 

B.	REQUIRE that the exercise of any contract option(s) for the purchase of Battery Electric Buses beyond the 220-bus base order (“Option Vehicles”) be subject to Board approval;

C.	DIRECT that the exercise of an option to purchase the remaining 1,600 Option Vehicles be structured for purposes of Board authorization in increments not to exceed 300 BEBs. The Board reserves the right to not exercise any option and to rebid the first option and any subsequent options presented; 

D.	Any request to the Board to approve the purchase of Option Vehicles shall include an evaluation regarding contractor’s performance with respect to the following;

1.	Adherence to established vehicle delivery timelines aligned with;

i. Fleet replacement requirements;
           ii. Depot electrification;
           iii. Infrastructure readiness;
           iv. Retirement schedules for aging compressed natural gas (CNG) buses; 

2.	Demonstrated operational reliability, range, efficiency, and technical performance of delivered BEBs in revenue service; and 

3.	Compliance with US Employment Program commitments, including: 

           i. Contract specific labor values forms
           ii. Job creation/retention metrics
           iii. Workforce training 
           iv. Commitment to hire disadvantage workers
           v. Certified payroll reporting 
           vi. Compliance with labor standards and Metro’s Manufacturing Careers Policy.
